  "verbalization": "Candesartan Cilexetil, an off-label use for Diastolic Heart Failure, is linked to Hypertension through a mechanism involving the off-label use of its off-label counterparts—Valsartan, Trandolapril, and Fosinopril. These drugs are commonly used to treat hypertension, suggesting a potential pathway where off-label use of Candesartan Cilexetil may contribute to the condition. The evidence is supported by the shared indication for Hypertension among the off-label uses of Candesartan Cilexetil and its off-label counterparts, indicating a possible mechanistic link through the modulation of blood pressure. The final scores suggest a strong, though not fully established, relationship, supported by the recurring use of these drugs in the context of hypertension. The integration of these paths highlights the potential for Candesartan Cilexetil to be repurposed for hypertension, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm the exact role.",
